    "blurb": "The show shines with a jazzy Eyes → Weather Report Suite sequence and an inspired Loser. Here Comes Sunshine and He's Gone are also highlights, and the band maintains high energy throughout.",
    "review": "September 26, 1973 at Buffalo's War Memorial Auditorium finds the Dead in fine form, delivering a setlist that moves from upbeat country‑rock to deep improvisational territory. The first set offers solid classics—Here Comes Sunshine, Deal, and a crisp China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider—but it's the second set that truly elevates the evening. A soaring Eyes of the World segues into a horn‑enhanced Weather Report Suite Prelude and Part 1, culminating in a fiery Let It Grow that showcases Jerry’s lyrical leads and Phil’s resonant bass. The band rides that momentum into a rousing Sugar Magnolia and wraps with an exuberant One More Saturday Night, leaving the audience buzzing. Across all available sources the performance feels tight yet adventurous, making this show a must‑listen for fans of the 1973 era.",
